# Per-device speed caps, one `config device` section each:
#
#	config device
#		option mac      '00:11:22:33:44:55'
#		option download '50'
#		option upload   '10'
#
# Megabits per second, and an absent option is no cap in that direction. A
# device's access rule — blocked outright, or off between two times — is a
# firewall rule in /etc/config/firewall, because that is what enforces it; the
# caps are here because a rate is a queueing discipline on the bridge and no
# firewall rule can express one.
